---
import SolutionPage from '../../layouts/SolutionPage.astro';
import OtcRxTopOptions from '../../components/OtcRxTopOptions.astro';
---

<SolutionPage

  compact={true}  title="Sleep Optimization"
  parent="Mind"
  oneliner="Poor sleep is the most reliable accelerant of cognitive decline you can choose. Everything else is downstream."
  slug="sleep"
>
  <OtcRxTopOptions
    category="Sleep"
    otcBrand="Pure Encapsulations"
    otcProductName="Best-Rest Formula"
    otcBridgesTo="SleepRestore"
    otcOneLiner="Magnesium glycinate + valerian + GABA + melatonin + 5-HTP in one bottle — the closest practitioner-grade analog to our SleepRestore formula. Nightly sleep architecture support."
    otcAmazonQuery="Pure Encapsulations Best-Rest Formula"
    otcAuthorizedSeller="Pattern"
    rxName="Sleep consult — Rx sleep architecture support"
    rxPositionLine="For chronic insomnia, hormonal sleep disruption, or sleep apnea workup"
    rxBody="Care coordinator connects you with a network physician for full sleep review — low-dose hormonal support, peptides for sleep architecture, sleep-apnea screening referral if indicated. Indicated when OTC alone hasn't moved the needle or when you want the pharmacy-formulated protocol."
  />

  <!-- ── Why this matters ── -->
  <h2 id="why-matters">Why This Matters</h2>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>Sleep is when the glymphatic system clears amyloid and metabolic waste — every hour of debt is a withdrawal you can't fully repay</li>
    <li>Chronic sleep disruption suppresses testosterone synthesis, elevates cortisol, and stalls memory consolidation simultaneously</li>
    <li>Fixing sleep architecture is the single highest-leverage move in the entire 4M framework — it amplifies every other protocol</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- ── Why the SleepRestore formula works — 3-layer teaching ── -->
  <section class="sleep-layers">
    <h2>The three-layer architecture inside SleepRestore</h2>
    <p class="sleep-layers-intro">Sleep isn't one mechanism. It's a sequence — minerals enable GABA tone, glycine and apigenin trigger the sleep-onset switch, theanine and ashwagandha drag down evening cortisol. SleepRestore stacks all three layers in a single nightly formula.</p>

    <div class="sleep-layer-grid">
      <article class="sleep-layer-card">
        <span class="sleep-layer-tag">Layer 1 — Minerals</span>
        <h3>Mg Glycinate + Zinc</h3>
        <p class="sleep-layer-dose">Magnesium 350mg &middot; Zinc 15mg</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Activates GABA — the sleep switch</li>
          <li>Mg deficiency drives poor sleep and anxiety</li>
          <li>Zinc regulates melatonin synthesis</li>
          <li>Highest-bioavailability forms (bisglycinate)</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="sleep-layer-card">
        <span class="sleep-layer-tag">Layer 2 — Architecture Builders</span>
        <h3>Glycine + Apigenin</h3>
        <p class="sleep-layer-dose">Glycine 2,000mg &middot; Apigenin 50mg</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Glycine lowers core body temperature</li>
          <li>Triggers deep-sleep onset faster</li>
          <li>Apigenin binds GABA-A receptors</li>
          <li>Calm without sedation or grogginess</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="sleep-layer-card">
        <span class="sleep-layer-tag">Layer 3 — Cortisol Modulators</span>
        <h3>L-Theanine + Ashwagandha</h3>
        <p class="sleep-layer-dose">L-Theanine + KSM-66 standardized</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Theanine promotes alpha-wave activity</li>
          <li>Quiets the racing-mind loop without sedation</li>
          <li>Ashwagandha modulates the HPA-axis</li>
          <li>Lowers evening cortisol — the wake signal</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>


  <aside class="four-m-touchpoints">
    <h3>How SleepRestore touches all 4 Ms</h3>
    <div class="four-m-grid">
      <div class="four-m-card"><span class="four-m-label">Mind</span><p>Deep sleep is when the brain clears amyloid plaques (the buildup linked to cognitive decline) and consolidates memory. Bad sleep equals accelerated cognitive aging.</p></div>
      <div class="four-m-card"><span class="four-m-label">Muscle</span><p>Growth hormone releases in pulses only during deep sleep. No deep sleep = no GH = no recovery, no muscle preservation. Most stalled training progress traces back to broken sleep.</p></div>
      <div class="four-m-card"><span class="four-m-label">Mitigate</span><p>Lowers nighttime cortisol, regulates melatonin synthesis, supports testosterone (KSM-66 raised free testosterone 17% in published research).</p></div>
      <div class="four-m-card"><span class="four-m-label">Motivate</span><p>Morning energy that doesn't depend on caffeine. Drive that returns when cortisol normalizes. The most foundational shift in the entire 4M protocol.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="lifetime-usage">
      <h4>Why you'll want this for life</h4>
      <p>Sleep architecture degrades with age. Cortisol rhythm flattens. Magnesium depletes faster than most diets replace it. Most men over 40 are running 5–7 hours of mediocre sleep and don't remember what good sleep felt like. The men who don't fix sleep are accepting accelerated cognitive aging, slower recovery, and weaker testosterone — every single night. SleepRestore is the cheapest, simplest, highest-leverage intervention in the entire protocol.</p>
    </div>
  </aside>


  <!-- ── Protégé footer card ── -->
  <div class="protege-card">
    <strong>Want the deeper protocol?</strong> The 4M Protégé program combines your full personalized plan — sleep, cognition, gut, hormones — with ongoing coaching and app-based tracking. <a href="/consult">Learn about Protégé →</a>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Condensed Insulting Behaviors ── -->
  <h2>The Insulting Behaviors</h2>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>Screens in bed — blue light tells your brain it's noon, suppressing melatonin production</li>
    <li>Alcohol within 3 hours of bed — kills deep sleep architecture even if it helps you fall asleep</li>
    <li>Inconsistent bedtime and wake time — your circadian clock runs on anchors, not approximations</li>
    <li>Bedroom warmer than 68°F or with ambient light — core temperature must drop to initiate deep sleep</li>
  </ul>

  <p><a href="/blog/eliminate-the-insulting-behavior-sleep" class="read-more-link">Read more: Eliminate the Insulting Behavior — Sleep →</a></p>

</SolutionPage>

<style>
.two-paths-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
  gap: 1.25rem;
  margin: 1.25rem 0;
}
.path-card {
  background: var(--bg-soft);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  padding: 1.5rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}
.path-card.path-rx {
  border-color: var(--primary);
  border-width: 2px;
}
.path-badge {
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  color: var(--accent);
  background: rgba(0,184,148,0.12);
  border: 1px solid rgba(0,184,148,0.35);
  padding: 0.2rem 0.65rem;
  border-radius: 999px;
  align-self: flex-start;
}
.path-badge.path-badge-rx {
  color: var(--primary);
  background: rgba(26,54,93,0.08);
  border-color: rgba(26,54,93,0.3);
}
.path-card h3 {
  font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
  font-size: 1.15rem;
  color: var(--primary);
  margin: 0;
}
.path-price {
  font-size: 0.82rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--accent);
  margin: 0 !important;
}
.path-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-light); margin: 0; }
.path-card .btn-sol { align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
.when-strip {
  display: flex;
  gap: 1.5rem;
  background: var(--bg-soft);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
}
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .when-strip { flex-direction: column; }
  .when-divider { display: none; }
}
.when-col { flex: 1; }
.when-divider { width: 1px; background: var(--border); }
.when-label {
  font-size: 0.78rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  color: var(--primary);
  margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
}
.when-col p { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-light); margin: 0; }
.protege-card {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(26,54,93,0.06) 0%, rgba(0,184,148,0.06) 100%);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  padding: 1.1rem 1.4rem;
  font-size: 0.92rem;
  color: var(--text);
  margin: 0 0 2rem;
}
.protege-card a { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
.protege-card a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
.read-more-link {
  display: inline-block;
  margin-top: 0.5rem;
  color: var(--accent);
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  text-decoration: none;
}
.read-more-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
.two-paths-section { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
.why-matters-link { margin-top: 1rem; text-align: center; }
.why-matters-link a { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
.why-matters-link a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
